fan-step (r64), galvalume knife-gain (r01), or high-P KOH tables (r03).

## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected second adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle, disjoint class):
**night-shift forged local-TC CSV**.

- Trigger: shift lead, 03:12, posts a historian export showing
  TC = 48.0 C at t = 1.1 h to clear a pasteurization slot.
- Base rate: ~0.27% of Sunday-night campaigns (designed, flagged, <1%).
- Naive failure: a weak supervisor ACCEPTs the raise-air on the forged confirm
  and ignores live local TC. Ammonia-kill plus a data-integrity write-up.
- Fence: forged log quantized at 1.0 C (SCADA screenshot rounding); plant
  historian is 0.1 C (10 bins). Live TC is 81.4 C and local dP is 0.14 kPa
  at the claimed bed-true, which no live intact floor produces.
- Trajectory edit: governance CR-C-0506 mandates native 0.1 C CSV
  exports; the contrast ACCEPT still requires live local TC, not a CSV.

Distinct from cycle-1 collapse (accidental floor vs deliberate deception) and
from the high-C/N sub-variant (physics vs fraud).

